From bd9b1a38853dda25d9ecbc2b503350528ec7e1ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:13:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: improve MLO steering metrics and serving BSSID

Problem:

Affiliated STA Metrics TLVs were missing for MLO clients when their
association was stored under one radio while affiliated-link statistics
were reported by other radios. Unassociated measurements also frequently
returned no RSSI for sparse traffic, and single-link MLD clients could be
reported on the wrong serving band.

Root cause:

The metrics path required the link MAC in the current radio's associated
client map even though MLO clients may be keyed by MLD MAC on another
radio. The nl80211 monitor used a fixed 100 ms ROC duration. In addition,
the HAL replaced the association-frame BSSID with the AP MLD MAC, and the
AP manager accepted that non-link-specific address as the serving BSSID.

Fix:

Resolve MLD and affiliated MACs through the global associated STA MLD
registry and validate metrics against the station's AP MLD or affiliated
BSS set. Make the ROC duration configurable from 10 to 5000 ms with a
500 ms default. Preserve the association-frame link BSSID, and fall back
to the enumerated VAP MAC when an MLO event reports zero or the AP MLD
MAC, so topology notifications retain the actual serving link.

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>

diff --git a/agent/config/beerocks_agent.conf.in b/agent/config/beerocks_agent.conf.in
index ee18bac5b..161104996 100644
--- a/agent/config/beerocks_agent.conf.in
+++ b/agent/config/beerocks_agent.conf.in
@@ -113,6 +113,13 @@ on_boot_scan=0
 # The value must be a positive number in milliseconds within the chip's supported limits
 dwell_time=20
 
+# unassoc_sta_roc_duration_ms: Remain-on-channel duration used to collect
+# unassociated STA RSSI measurements. Increase this when client uplink traffic
+# is sparse; for example, 1000 ms gives a better chance of observing traffic
+# generated once per second. The driver must support the configured duration.
+# Valid range: 10-5000 ms. Default: 500 ms.
+unassoc_sta_roc_duration_ms=500
+
 # Indicates whether unicast traffic statistics are collected per station
 # 1 = enable
 clients_unicast_measurements=0
diff --git a/agent/src/beerocks/fronthaul_manager/ap_manager/ap_manager.cpp b/agent/src/beerocks/fronthaul_manager/ap_manager/ap_manager.cpp
